# Auto-commit policy (agnishashwat repos)

The owner has granted standing permission to commit **and push automatically** in this
repository without asking first.

- Commit and push completed, coherent units of work to `origin/main` without prompting
  for confirmation.
- Use the `agnishashwat` GitHub identity. The repo's local git config is set to
  `agnishashwat <277563858+agnishashwat@users.noreply.github.com>`. If `gh`'s active
  account is not `agnishashwat`, switch it: `gh auth switch --user agnishashwat`.
- Write clear commit messages: imperative subject line, with the "why" in the body.
- Group related changes into one logical commit; keep unrelated changes in separate ones.

## Still ask first for

- Destructive/irreversible git operations (force push, hard reset, history rewrite,
  branch or tag deletion).
- Changing repo visibility or deleting the remote.
- Committing files that may contain secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
